comments.body:
@vvo 

> I have carefully read the test diff but fail to see where we missed the count? Only thing I see is that the datastructure for hierarchical facet was not the same than the others (missing {name, count}).

For the tests, I wasn't using the same data structure than what the helper was sending.

I was using

``` js
hierarchicalFacets: [{
  name: 'hierarchicalFacet1',
    data: {
      hierarchicalFacet1val1: 4
    }
  }
}]
```

Where in fact, the helper would send back

``` js
hierarchicalFacets: [{
  name: 'hierarchicalFacet1',
    data: {
      hierarchicalFacet1val1: {name: 'hierarchicalFacet1val1', count: 4}
    }
  }
}]
```

So the test worked, but not in real life, where the helper wouldn't actually send data like this.

> > It now only returns the last value
> 
> Can you precise what do you mean here?

Sure : instead of returning "Cat > Subcat > Subsubcat", I now only returns "SubSubCat". It's ok, since this function is only used for `clearAll` and `currentRefinedValues`.
This is to avoid having "Long Category Name > Long subcategory Name > ..." in the list.
